    "abstract": "A combination of results on the rare $B_{s}^{0} \\\\to \\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}$ and $B^{0} \\\\to \\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}$ decays from the ATLAS, CMS, and LHCb experiments using data collected at the Large Hadron Collider between 2011 and 2016, is presented. The $B_{s}^{0} \\\\to \\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}$ branching fraction is obtained to be $\\\\mathcal{B}(B_{s}^{0}\\\\to\\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}) = (2.69_{-0.35}^{+0.37}) \\\\times 10^{-9}$ and the ratio $\\\\mathcal{B}(B^{0}\\\\to\\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-})/\\\\mathcal{B}(B_{s}^{0}\\\\to\\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}) < 0.060$ at 95% CL. The effective lifetime of the $B_{s}^{0} \\\\to \\\\mu^{+}\\\\mu^{-}$ decay is measured to be $\\\\tau_{\\\\rm eff} = 1.91_{-0.35}^{+0.37}$ ps.",
